**High \(p_{\perp}\) Inclusive Charged Hadron Distributions in Au+Au Collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{NN}}}=130\) GeV at RHIC**

Publication No.

Bum Jin Choi, Ph.D.

The University of Texas at Austin, 2003

Supervisors: Fred Moore

Peter Jacobs

This thesis reports the measurement of the inclusive charged particle (\(h^{+}+h^{-}\)) p\({}_{\perp}\) spectra for \(1.7<p_{\perp}<6\) GeV/c at midrapidity (\(|\eta|<0.5\)) as a function of various centrality classes in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{{}_{\rm NN}}}\)=130 GeV. Hadron suppression is observed relative to both scaled NN and peripheral Au+Au reference data, possibly indicating non-Abelian radiative energy loss in a hot, dense medium.

